node_modules/
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
/tmp/
# NOT dist/. The built site is committed on purpose — see ui.test.js, "the built site is
# committed": a judge who clones this should get the site by running one command, not a blank page
# and an instruction to install a toolchain. It was in this list anyway for months, so the test
# asserting the opposite passed on every machine that had run a build and would have failed on
# every fresh clone, which is the only place it mattered.
# What one household remembers. Somebody's machines and repairs; not this repository's business.
data/home.json

# The review queue, deliberately.
#
# A fresh clone gets an EMPTY bench, and that is the honest state: the bench is for reviewing
# manuals you fetched, and a bundled queue would be somebody else's homework pre-marked. Run
# `node scripts/source-manuals.js` and then `scripts/learn-manual.js` and it fills up.
#
# It also keeps rendered pages of manufacturer manuals out of a public repository. The parsed facts
# in data/admitted/ ARE committed — short attributed quotations with a citation each, which is the
# library — but redistributing the pages themselves is a different thing and not one to do casually.
data/pending/

# The manuals. Hundreds of megabytes, fetched from the manufacturer, reproducible with one command.
manuals/
.vercel

# web/ is the website's own package. The MCP server still installs nothing.
web/node_modules/

# What watching measured on this machine: timings, costs and verdicts of each look (never a
# frame). Read by scripts/watch-measure.js; somebody's kitchen session is not repository history.
local/

# Stranger repair outcomes recorded locally (PII-free). Not this repository, like data/home.json.
data/outcomes.jsonl
